<title>SWITZERLAND: Tietmeyer says G-10 sees no inflation problem.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says G-10 sees no inflation problem.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said inflation in Europe was not a current problem despite a rise of import prices.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters at the monthly Group of 10 meeting of central banker chiefs, Tietmeyer also said the central bankers were happy there was no spillover effect from import prices on the general price level.</p>
<p>&quot;Inflation does not seem to be a new problem until now in spite of import prices rising in a lot of countries,&quot; Tietmeyer said referring to continental Europe.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
